    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0414" n="332" xml:id="pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 895.00/539.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-02-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1296.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of my note (No. 525) to the minister for foreign affairs, dated the 2d instant,
                    on the subject of the transfer to the proper courts at Seoul of criminal
                    proceedings against American citizens in Chosen; also a copy of the note (No. 6)
                    in reply, dated the 6th instant. These notes, in conjunction with my telegram of
                        yesterday<anchor n="1" xml:id="d427-f1"/> will put the Department in
                    possession of the manner in which the matter has been disposed of. I venture to
                    hope that my action will have the approval of the Department.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. J. O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d427-a1.xml" xpointer="d427-a1"/>
